{
  "description": "An architecture-aware diagnostic adapter for Self-EvolveRec that measures a trained recommender’s behavior and supplies those measurements, with definitions, to an interpretation prompt. It preserves the native diagnostic interface while using RecHarness macro-average validation HR@10 for model selection across all four Amazon datasets.",
  "motivation": "Support evidence-based model improvements while keeping diagnostics compatible with the trained architecture, available public data, and the fixed benchmark. Diagnostic observations guide hypotheses; validation HR@10 determines whether changes help.",
  "implementation_notes": "Retain DiagnosisProbe(view, device), run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), and diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis). Return metrics and metric_definitions, and build the interpretation prompt from actual measurements. Probe view.model as the trained nn.Module through the compatibility methods item_emb, log2feats, and predict_score. Handle B x L sequence, positive, and negative tensors, masking padding. Adapt probes whenever the architecture changes. Use only interaction histories, titles, descriptions, and timestamps; ratings, review text, commercial metadata, and simulator diversity/conformity traits are unavailable. Generate full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for twenty real training users, five per dataset. Preserve dataset routing, preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, DATA_DIR=os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], and trial-local artifacts. Update the predictor writer when changing inference. No measured results are supplied, so effectiveness is unverified.",
  "pseudocode": "probe = DiagnosisProbe(view, device)\nraw_diagnosis = probe.run_full_diagnosis(train_loader)\nassert raw_diagnosis contains metrics and metric_definitions\nprompt = diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis)\nhypotheses = interpret_measured_evidence(prompt)\nfor authorized candidate within the shared search budget:\n    train candidate using the fixed data splits and seeds\n    adapt probes and predictor writer to its architecture\n    obtain pinned validation HR@10 for each dataset\n    selection_score = mean(the four dataset HR@10 values)\nselect candidate by selection_score without accessing test labels",
  "originality": {
    "score": 4,
    "positive": "Connects architecture-aware diagnostics and an interpretation prompt within a controlled recommendation search workflow.",
    "negative": "The description specifies an adapter contract rather than a new recommendation algorithm or novel diagnostic statistic. Score uses a 1–10 scale."
  },
  "future_potential": {
    "score": 7,
    "positive": "Could make iterative changes more interpretable and expose architecture-specific failures using reproducible measurements.",
    "negative": "Benefits depend on probe quality and whether diagnostic hypotheses improve validation performance within the search budget; no supporting results are provided."
  },
  "code_difficulty": {
    "score": 5,
    "positive": "The fixed interface and defined batch format give a clear implementation boundary.",
    "negative": "Correct masking, architecture adaptation, full-catalog recommendation, and agreement between training and generated inference require careful integration. Higher scores indicate greater difficulty."
  }
}
